                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Manufacturing ERP" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Manufacturing ERP" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Manufacturing ERP Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>Manufacturing organizations may struggle with disconnected systems, duplicate data, manual processes, limited visibility, and inconsistent operational workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Disconnected Business Systems: Integrate core manufacturing and business processes through a centralized ERP platform.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Manual Data Entry: Automate repetitive transactions and workflow activities to reduce manual effort.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Limited Operational Visibility: Create centralized dashboards and reports for production, inventory, purchasing, and business performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Inconsistent Processes: Standardize workflows, approvals, and operating procedures across teams.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Difficult Reporting: Use structured data, dashboards, and analytics to provide timely operational insights.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Manufacturing ERP</b></h3>
                <p>Manufacturers have different production models, approval processes, inventory structures, and reporting requirements. Customization helps the ERP support these unique processes.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Customize Production Workflows: Configure ERP processes around production planning, work orders, and manufacturing operations.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Create Role-Based Workspaces: Provide production, inventory, procurement, finance, and management teams with relevant actions and information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Automate Approvals: Configure automated approvals, alerts, notifications, and operational tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Build Custom Dashboards: Provide role-specific insights into production, inventory, procurement, and financial performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Gather User Feedback: Continuously improve ERP workflows based on user feedback and business results.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

